{
  "id": "power-budget",
  "title": "Power Budget",
  "arc": 1,
  "stages": [
    {
      "type": "briefing",
      "lines": [
        "Every part of Rover eats energy. The battery is the fuel tank.",
        "Today you learn to count how much each part eats, and how long Rover will run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "toy": {
        "kind": "battery-life",
        "prompt": "Change the battery size and how hungry the robot is. Watch the hours."
      },
      "chunks": {
        "1": [
          "A big [[capacity]] battery lasts longer. A hungry robot drains it faster.",
          "[[power]] is how hungry a part is, measured in watts (W).",
          "Count up the power of every part and you know what the battery must supply."
        ],
        "2": [
          "[[capacity]] is in milliamp-hours (mAh). Divide it by the [[current]] the robot draws in [[milliamp]] and you get hours.",
          "[[power]] = [[voltage]] × [[current]], in watts (W)."
        ],
        "3": [
          "[[power]] P = V × I, in watts. Energy used = P × time. Run time ≈ [[capacity]] (mAh) ÷ [[current]] (mA), less in practice.",
          "Very small and very large quantities are written in standard form: 3.2 × 10⁻³ A is 3.2 [[milliamp]]."
        ]
      },
      "help": {
        "1": "Big battery = long time. Hungry robot = short time.",
        "2": "A fuel tank: a big tank and a thirsty engine. Time = tank ÷ thirst.",
        "3": "Try 2000 mAh and 200 mA. That is 10 hours.",
        "4": "Slide each slider and watch the hours. The rule is on the screen."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "formula": "power",
      "intro": {
        "1": "Push × flow is how hungry a part is.",
        "2": "[[power]] in watts is [[voltage]] times [[current]]. Into the Formula Book.",
        "3": "P = VI. Into the Formula Book."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example",
      "steps": {
        "1": [
          "Rover's motor: 6 V push, 2 A flow.",
          "Power = push × flow.",
          "6 × 2 = 12.",
          "The motor uses 12 W."
        ],
        "3": [
          "V = 6 V, I = 2 A.",
          "P = V × I = 6 × 2.",
          "P = 12 W.",
          "In one hour it uses 12 Wh of energy."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "try",
      "title": "Try one",
      "questions": [
        {
          "prompt": {
            "1": "A part runs on {V} V and draws {I} A. How many watts does it use?",
            "2": "A part runs on {V} V and draws {I} A. How many watts does it use?",
            "3": "A part runs on {V} V and draws {I} mA. How many watts does it use?"
          },
          "unit": "W",
          "gen": {
            "1": {
              "vars": {
                "V": {
                  "pick": [
                    3,
                    6,
                    9,
                    12
                  ]
                },
                "I": {
                  "pick": [
                    1,
                    2,
                    3
                  ]
                }
              },
              "answer": "V * I"
            },
            "2": {
              "vars": {
                "V": {
                  "pick": [
                    3,
                    4.5,
                    6,
                    9
                  ]
                },
                "I": {
                  "pick": [
                    0.1,
                    0.2,
                    0.5,
                    1.5
                  ]
                }
              },
              "answer": "V * I",
              "dp": 3
            },
            "3": {
              "vars": {
                "V": {
                  "pick": [
                    3,
                    4.5,
                    6,
                    9
                  ]
                },
                "I": {
                  "pick": [
                    50,
                    120,
                    250,
                    500
                  ]
                }
              },
              "answer": "V * I / 1000",
              "dp": 3
            }
          },
          "explain": {
            "1": "P = V × I = {V} × {I} = {answer} W.",
            "2": "P = V × I = {V} × {I} = {answer} W.",
            "3": "P = V × I = {V} × ({I} ÷ 1000) = {answer} W."
          },
          "wrong": [
            {
              "expr": "V / I",
              "why": "Power is push × flow, so multiply."
            }
          ],
          "hints": [
            "Look up power in the Formula Book.",
            "P = V × I.",
            "{V} times the flow."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "help": {
        "1": "Push times flow.",
        "2": "Like cost = price × amount.",
        "3": "Example: 6 V × 2 A = 12 W.",
        "4": "Watch: multiply {V} by the flow. Then add the unit, watts."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "formula": "battery-life",
      "intro": {
        "1": "How long will it last? Size of the tank divided by how fast you drain it.",
        "2": "Run time = [[capacity]] ÷ [[current]]. Into the Formula Book.",
        "3": "hours = mAh ÷ mA. Into the Formula Book."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "try",
      "title": "Try battery life",
      "questions": [
        {
          "prompt": {
            "1": "A {cap} mAh battery. The robot draws {d} mA. How many hours does it last?",
            "2": "A {cap} mAh battery. The robot draws {d} mA. How many hours does it last?",
            "3": "A {cap} mAh battery. The motors draw {a} mA and the lights {b} mA. How many hours does it last?"
          },
          "unit": "h",
          "gen": {
            "1": {
              "vars": {
                "cap": {
                  "pick": [
                    1000,
                    2000,
                    3000
                  ]
                },
                "d": {
                  "pick": [
                    100,
                    200,
                    500,
                    1000
                  ]
                }
              },
              "answer": "cap / d",
              "where": [
                "cap / d == round(cap / d)"
              ]
            },
            "2": {
              "vars": {
                "cap": {
                  "pick": [
                    1000,
                    1500,
                    2000,
                    2500,
                    3000
                  ]
                },
                "d": {
                  "pick": [
                    120,
                    150,
                    200,
                    250,
                    400
                  ]
                }
              },
              "answer": "cap / d",
              "dp": 1
            },
            "3": {
              "vars": {
                "cap": {
                  "pick": [
                    2000,
                    2500,
                    3000,
                    5000
                  ]
                },
                "a": {
                  "pick": [
                    150,
                    200,
                    300
                  ]
                },
                "b": {
                  "pick": [
                    50,
                    100
                  ]
                }
              },
              "answer": "cap / (a + b)",
              "dp": 1
            }
          },
          "explain": {
            "1": "hours = capacity ÷ current = {cap} ÷ {d} = {answer} h.",
            "2": "hours = capacity ÷ current = {cap} ÷ {d} = {answer} h.",
            "3": "Total draw = {a} + {b} mA. hours = {cap} ÷ ({a} + {b}) = {answer} h."
          },
          "wrong": [
            {
              "expr": "cap * 1",
              "why": "Divide the battery size by what the robot uses."
            }
          ],
          "hints": [
            "hours = capacity ÷ current.",
            "Make sure both are in milliamps.",
            "Divide the big number by the small one."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
